 GLB validation checks binary/accessor bounds, finite geometry, degenerate triangles, authored normals, collapsed/missing UVs, missing external textures, weights, joint indices, inverse-bind counts and animation time ordering. It does not certify topology quality, internal visibility, deformation or watertightness. Visual acceptance is bound to the runtime hash. Source and runtime artifacts can be downloaded separately without labeling them production ready.
+
+## Whole-game quality and performance calibration
+
+The current integrated diagnosis/repair interface is available at **http://127.0.0.1:8742**. Older task instances were stopped. Restart the normal launcher to use its usual port. See [the installed diagnosis and replacement workflow](docs/diagnosis_repair.md).
+
+Measured against the real Ironfield outdoor scene at 1920 x 1080 on this GTX 1080/i7-5820K: ordinary grouped creatures use a 12,000-triangle target; the main rider retains its 42,000-triangle mesh because rendering has headroom and the 30,000-triangle trial loses coat/hand detail. Rare creatures retain approximately 14,000 triangles. Static reductions that damage the silhouette retain their source. This is a calibration for this game, scene density and hardware, not a universal mesh budget.
+
+See [the whole-game measurements and opened Godot comparisons](D:/Games/Metin2Clone/docs/asset_optimization/README.md). Each isolated optimization study retains its imported source, frozen settings, original generation lineage, Blender reports and runtime export in the library. Technical validation leaves visual acceptance pending.
+
